kupferdraht-core/proto/generic_message.proto is a modified subset of
Wire's GenericMessage schema
(https://github.com/wireapp/generic-message-proto), which Wire Swiss
GmbH publishes under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or (at
your option) any later version. Wire's notice, as reproduced from the
copy that wireapp/kalium vendors at revision 9ccecabb, and Kupferdraht's
modification notice are in that file. The subset is distributed under
GPL-3.0-only as part of Kupferdraht, as the or-later grant permits.

Attribution policy: where Wire's work is incorporated, Kupferdraht
keeps Wire's notice, as the schema above shows. Anyone who finds Wire's
expression elsewhere in this tree without such a notice is asked to
report it to opensource@digits.schwarz; the notice will be added.

Sources: Kupferdraht is written from Wire's published API description
(the OpenAPI document every wire-server deployment serves), RFC 9420
and live observation of self-hosted wire-server deployments. Wire's
open-source repositories, chiefly wireapp/kalium at revision 9ccecabb,
were read to observe protocol behaviour; every such reading is listed
with its source in docs/wire/kalium-readings.md. The Proteus prekey
format is implemented from its public specification; the public API
follows the conceptual model of matrix-rust-sdk (below).

